    "title": "H3 nonidentity P25 subresultant scalar compiler",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For F_n(X)=((1-X)^n-1)/X and G_n(T,X)=X^(n-1)F_n(T/X), specialization at T=t has gcd degree exactly P(t). The coefficient ideal of polynomial subresultants 0 through 24, saturated by (T-1)Y=1, has a finite scalar annihilator whose odd-prime support is exactly the characteristics admitting a nonidentity P>=25 fiber. This starts from two sparse degree-n-1 polynomials but makes no elimination-cost or factorization claim.",
